By application, hospital settings lead due to the complexity of chemotherapy, targeted therapy, and transfusion-based treatments.
By end user, adults represent the largest patient group, driven by higher prevalence of hematologic cancers.
By disease indication, leukemia and lymphoma account for the largest share, supported by continuous therapeutic innovation.
By therapeutic approach, targeted therapy is emerging as the dominant segment, reflecting a decisive move toward precision medicine.
